    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d434">

                <pb facs="0508" n="448" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg448"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr.
                            Runyon</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-12-07"><hi rendition="#italic">December 7,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 490.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to a letter of this date,
                    inclosing a communication from the governor of the State of New York, together
                    with copies of communications from the superintendent of insurance of the State
                    of Missouri, I send you herewith copy of letter to this Department from
                    superintendent of insurance of the State of New York, from which it <pb
                        facs="0509" n="449" xml:id="pg449"/> appears that he has requested Mr.
                    Poultney Bigelow to act as his representative with the proper officers of the
                    Kingdom of Prussia in reference to the subject-matter of his letter.</p>
                <p>Please do anything in your power to facilitate the objects of Mr. Bigelow’s
                    mission, by giving him access to the proper Prussian officials or otherwise.</p>
                <p>Respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
